# Phase 8g (cvvdp-fork, 2026-05-25) — per-block tile_dist distribution capture

## Inputs
- harness: `jxl-encoder/examples/cvvdp_phase8g_tile_dist_capture.rs`
- env hook: `JXL_PHASE8G_TILE_DIST_DUMP=<path>` →
  `maybe_dump_tile_dist_stats_phase8g` in `vardct/perceptual_loop.rs`
- fixtures: 5 (CID22 1025469/1418519/1189261, GB82-SC terminal/imac_g3)
- distances: {0.5, 1.0, 2.0, 3.0}
- effort: 8 (buttloop fires)
- backends: butter (CPU butteraugli) + cvvdp (GPU cvvdp, Phase 8c renorm
  active scale = 0.018)
- iters per encode: 3 → 4 rows per (image, distance, backend) cell
- total rows: 5 × 4 × 2 × 3 = 120 + 1 header

## Schema
- `tag`: `corpus|name|d=DIST|backend=BACKEND`
- `backend`: `butter | cvvdp`
- `iter`: 0..3 (0 = seed iter, drives largest qac adjustment)
- `effective_target`: per-backend target (butter = `target_distance`,
  cvvdp = `cvvdp_target_score_for_distance(target_distance)` lookup)
- `target_distance`: the bitstream quality target (always butteraugli-direction)
- `nblocks`: width_blocks × height_blocks at this image size
- `td_min` / `td_max` / `td_median` / `td_p25` / `td_p75` / `td_p95`:
  per-block tile_dist distribution stats post per-block 16th-power-norm
  reduction (matches libjxl TileDistMap)
- `td_mean`: mean of tile_dist values
- `bad_rate`: fraction of blocks where `tile_dist > effective_target`
  — the `diff > 1.0` predicate fire rate that drives bad-block qac
  tightening in the seed loop

## Headline finding (this commit, pre-fit cvvdp = `k_tile_norm = 1.2`)

For CID22 photos at iter=0:
- butter `bad_rate` = 0.0% to 13% depending on distance
- cvvdp `bad_rate` = 70% to 100% — driving qac UP on most blocks per iter
- cvvdp `td_mean` ~14.7× SMALLER than butter (mean ratio b/c on iter=0:
  median = 14.7 across 20 cells)
- post-renorm cvvdp `td_p95 / target` ratios cluster at 2.4-3.9
  (butter's are 0.5-0.8)

Mechanism: Phase 8c renorm aligns per-pixel `diffmap.mean()` between
backends, but the 16th-power norm `(Σ v^16 / n)^(1/16)` is a max-norm
proxy. For butteraugli's peaked distribution (narrow high-energy
regions) the norm ≈ max(v). For cvvdp's broader distribution (Laplacian
pyramid + per-band CSF smearing), the norm is much smaller than max(v).
Phase 8c's mean-alignment leaves a ~6-15× gap on the post-reduction
ratio, which the bad-block predicate AMPLIFIES into a 70-100% vs 0-13%
fire-rate divergence.

## Per-distance bad_rate (pre-fit, median across 5 fixtures)

| d | butter | cvvdp | ratio (b/c) |
|---|---|---|---|
| 0.5 | 0.037 | 0.93 | 0.039 |
| 1.0 | 0.001 | 0.70 | 0.001 |
| 2.0 | 0.000 | 0.80 | 0.000 |
| 3.0 | 0.000 | 0.88 | 0.000 |

## Fit derivation

Per RFC §3.2 Intervention A (linear scale per constant): we want cvvdp's
`td_p95 / target` to approach butter's near-zero `bad_rate`. Specifically,
shift cvvdp's `td_p95` to near `effective_target` — gives ~5% bad_rate
post-fit.

Per-distance scale needed:
| d | cvvdp_p95 | target | scale_to_align |
|---|---|---|---|
| 0.5 | 0.028 | 0.0029 | 0.104 |
| 1.0 | 0.105 | 0.0238 | 0.227 |
| 2.0 | 0.49 | 0.0724 | 0.148 |
| 3.0 | 1.39 | 0.1336 | 0.096 |

Median across distances: ~0.13. Shipped median * 1.2 ≈ **0.16** as the
single-value `CVVDP_BLOCK_CONSTANTS.k_tile_norm`.

## Post-fit validation (re-captured at `k_tile_norm = 0.16`)

Post-fit per-distance bad_rate (from
`benchmarks/cvvdp_block_signal_distribution_postfit_2026-05-25.tsv`):

| d | butter | cvvdp_post_fit | parity? |
|---|---|---|---|
| 0.5 | 0.037 | 0.032 | YES |
| 1.0 | 0.001 | 0.002 | YES |
| 2.0 | 0.000 | 0.002 | YES |
| 3.0 | 0.000 | 0.003 | YES |

The fit achieves bad_rate parity across all distance bands. The end-to-end
Pareto bench (`benchmarks/cvvdp_phase8g_pareto_2026-05-25.tsv`) confirms
this translates to **85.0% Pareto-front position**, meeting the ≥85%
ship target.

## Reproduce
```bash
JXL_PHASE8G_TILE_DIST_DUMP=/tmp/cvvdp_p8g_tile_dist.tsv \
  cargo run --release -p jxl-encoder \
  --features '__expert butteraugli-loop cvvdp-loop ssim2-loop parallel' \
  --example cvvdp_phase8g_tile_dist_capture -- \
  --dump-out /tmp/cvvdp_p8g_tile_dist.tsv \
  --out benchmarks/cvvdp_block_signal_distribution_2026-05-25.tsv
```

## DO NOT
- DO NOT cite "FMA precision" for the per-iter bad_rate disparity.
  This is a structural distribution-shape effect of the 16th-power norm
  reduction, documented above.
- DO NOT remove the `JXL_PHASE8G_TILE_DIST_DUMP` env hook — it is the
  measurement infrastructure for future per-distance refinement
  (Phase 8h candidate per RFC §3.4 if the single-value Phase 8g fit
  proves insufficient on out-of-corpus content).
- DO NOT widen the fit corpus from these 5 fixtures without also
  validating the W44 cost-model gates don't shift their classification
  decisions — the dispatchers (W44-91, W44-96, W44-176) consume the
  same `mask1x1` field as the per-block reducer and could route
  affected cells through different code paths.
